## Summary
Marco Balich, known as the grand ceremony master of the Olympics, shares anecdotes about his past, including being a DJ at De Michelis' parties and keeping Peter Gabriel and Yoko Ono at bay in Turin. He also mentions earning 18 million for an Indian wedding at Borgo Egnazia and leaves his potential candidacy for Mayor of Venice open.

## Key Points
- Marco Balich was a DJ at parties hosted by De Michelis.
- He claims to have kept Peter Gabriel and Yoko Ono at a distance during an event in Turin.
- Earned 18 million for organizing an Indian wedding at Borgo Egnazia.
- Leaves open the possibility of running for Mayor of Venice.


